# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Agent runtime state: synapse_checkpoint.py writes resume checkpoints to
# agent/checkpoints/ (CHECKPOINT_DIR). That is per-session runtime data, never
# source. Tests are hermetic -- they monkeypatch CHECKPOINT_DIR to a tmp_path.
agent/checkpoints/

# Test pollution: tests/test_retina_manifest.py writes to a path derived from a
# MagicMock repr when it runs without a real Houdini, dropping a file literally
# named "<MagicMock name='mock.retina_manifest.json" in the repo root on every
# headless suite run. Ignored so it cannot ride along in a commit; the real fix
# is to make that test write under tmp_path.
<MagicMock*
*.so
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.egg

